WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.022
- What would you do for a donut?

00:00:02.022 --> 00:00:03.266
- Kill a man.

00:00:03.266 --> 00:00:05.933
(Andrew laughs)

00:00:07.194 --> 00:00:08.978
- Adam, Andrew,

00:00:08.978 --> 00:00:11.228
you all ready for season 2?

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.053
- Yeah.

00:00:14.189 --> 00:00:15.244
- Let's do it.

00:00:15.244 --> 00:00:17.551
We're going to open up
this season with a bang.

00:00:17.551 --> 00:00:19.170
And that bang is donuts.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.992
Today we're going to have three donuts

00:00:20.992 --> 00:00:23.006
at three drastically
different price points,

00:00:23.006 --> 00:00:24.673
to find out which one
is the most worth it,

00:00:24.673 --> 00:00:25.702
at its price.

00:00:25.702 --> 00:00:27.522
This season may be the season

00:00:27.522 --> 00:00:29.522
that people call the Gold Season.

00:00:29.522 --> 00:00:30.668
- The Golden Years?

00:00:30.668 --> 00:00:31.652
- The Golden Boys.

00:00:31.652 --> 00:00:32.868
That's who we should be.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:35.571
I've heard that if you eat
gold, you also poop gold.

00:00:35.571 --> 00:00:37.687
- I don't become a little bit more gold?

00:00:37.687 --> 00:00:39.437
- No, you excrete it.

00:00:40.346 --> 00:00:41.559
- Don't love that word.

00:00:41.559 --> 00:00:43.135
- You ready for donut number one?

00:00:43.135 --> 00:00:45.968
- I am ready for donut number one.

00:00:47.007 --> 00:00:48.674
All right, let's go.

00:00:53.485 --> 00:00:54.609
- Hi, my name is Teresa.

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:56.176
I'm the owner of Blinkie's
Donuts in Woodland Hills.

00:00:56.176 --> 00:00:58.079
And I'm really happy to be here.

00:00:58.079 --> 00:00:59.342
- [Andrew] You've been here since?

00:00:59.342 --> 00:01:00.347
- [Teresa] 2002.

00:01:00.347 --> 00:01:02.179
- [Andrew] And is this
a family business, or?

00:01:02.179 --> 00:01:03.329
- Yes, my uncle was baking today.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:04.624
Mom's at the register,

00:01:04.624 --> 00:01:06.279
my son, she won't let go to the register.

00:01:06.279 --> 00:01:07.980
Everybody's part of the Team Blinkies.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:09.355
We're all a big, happy family.

00:01:09.355 --> 00:01:11.680
Today, we're going to have
a regular glazed donut,

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:13.635
that's the most popular one that we sell.

00:01:13.635 --> 00:01:14.812
It's very simple.

00:01:14.812 --> 00:01:17.592
We're just going to start with
a regular yeast donut dough,

00:01:17.592 --> 00:01:19.063
mix it, put it in a proofer,

00:01:19.063 --> 00:01:20.644
cut it, proof it again,

00:01:20.644 --> 00:01:23.736
fry, and glaze with our
regular glaze icing.

00:01:23.736 --> 00:01:25.600
- [Andrew] How do your
donuts differ from sort of

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:27.509
the mass-produced donuts,
in terms of flavor?

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:29.183
- [Teresa] We just try to find
the best ingredients we can

00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:31.314
that's available on the market,

00:01:31.314 --> 00:01:32.840
and also make it budget friendly,

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.393
so that everybody can come in,

00:01:34.393 --> 00:01:36.511
and afford a donut at our place.

00:01:36.511 --> 00:01:39.397
- This is the encyclopedia
picture of a donut.

00:01:39.397 --> 00:01:40.897
Let's bump donuts.

00:01:45.623 --> 00:01:47.480
It's like the inside of a croissant.

00:01:47.480 --> 00:01:48.589
That's amazing.

00:01:48.589 --> 00:01:49.871
- It's so fluffy.

00:01:49.871 --> 00:01:52.072
- My finger just disappears
inside this thing.

00:01:52.072 --> 00:01:54.328
- It's a very gentle
donut eating experience.

00:01:54.328 --> 00:01:58.894
This is truly the best
donut I have ever had.

00:01:58.894 --> 00:02:00.528
- [Teresa] So the black and
white is really popular.

00:02:00.528 --> 00:02:01.741
It's like a glazed donut.

00:02:01.741 --> 00:02:02.695
This is same dough.

00:02:02.695 --> 00:02:04.900
Fry, and then we just let
it cool down a little bit,

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.683
and then we put on vanilla icing,

00:02:06.683 --> 00:02:07.924
and our chocolate icing,

00:02:07.924 --> 00:02:08.832
which is a secret recipe.

00:02:08.832 --> 00:02:10.141
- [Andrew] You were saying you use

00:02:10.141 --> 00:02:11.171
a lot of different kinds of chocolates,

00:02:11.171 --> 00:02:12.180
why is that?
- Yes, we used five different

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.305
types of chocolate.

00:02:13.305 --> 00:02:14.993
We're quite picky on our chocolate tastes.

00:02:14.993 --> 00:02:16.222
And we want to make sure that

00:02:16.222 --> 00:02:17.490
our customer feel the same way,

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.686
and have the best experience.

00:02:18.686 --> 00:02:20.106
- They call it the black and white donut.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:24.106
But others call it the
V, or the Batman, or the,

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:26.228
tuxedo.

00:02:27.586 --> 00:02:28.753
- I like this.

00:02:31.376 --> 00:02:34.267
The icing on most donuts
can be overwhelming.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:38.394
But actually, it adds a
perfect kick to the donut.

00:02:38.394 --> 00:02:40.461
- [Andrew] It's got that same great base.

00:02:40.461 --> 00:02:41.803
- [Steven] And that chocolate is so rich.

00:02:41.803 --> 00:02:42.957
- The chocolate really is good.

00:02:42.957 --> 00:02:44.333
Because you only get that streak,

00:02:44.333 --> 00:02:45.685
you can really enjoy it,

00:02:45.685 --> 00:02:47.224
and pick your bite a little more.

00:02:47.224 --> 00:02:49.232
It's not overwhelmingly chocolatey.

00:02:49.232 --> 00:02:50.556
- I thought the streak was weird at first,

00:02:50.556 --> 00:02:52.866
but I like that it's only
covering a little bit.

00:02:52.866 --> 00:02:54.523
- Steven thought it was weird.

00:02:54.523 --> 00:02:56.091
- I don't think it was weird.
- I'm telling.

00:02:56.091 --> 00:02:57.507
- Yeah, go ahead.

00:02:57.507 --> 00:02:58.439
Oh my God.

00:02:58.439 --> 00:02:59.591
- I need to stop myself.

00:02:59.591 --> 00:03:02.091
Adam, would you like a sample?

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:05.049
You like that?

00:03:05.049 --> 00:03:06.669
Go ahead and take the rest.

00:03:06.669 --> 00:03:08.321
- That's the stuff.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:11.071
(Andrew singing)

00:03:13.093 --> 00:03:15.549
I don't know how anybody
can beat that donut.

00:03:15.549 --> 00:03:17.938
Just based on value, experience,

00:03:17.938 --> 00:03:19.623
quality of donut,

00:03:19.623 --> 00:03:21.285
like it had everything.

00:03:21.285 --> 00:03:22.960
- Watching her uncle work,

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:24.497
that guy is a straight donut wizard.

00:03:24.497 --> 00:03:25.886
The Donut-dore.

00:03:25.886 --> 00:03:27.280
- The Donut Dumbledore.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:29.207
- Dumble Dorenut.

00:03:29.207 --> 00:03:30.265
Dumbledonut.

00:03:30.265 --> 00:03:31.658
Yeah, Dumbledonut.

00:03:31.658 --> 00:03:33.459
I'm ready for a light and airy donut fact.

00:03:33.459 --> 00:03:34.603
- [Steven] Donut Fact.

00:03:34.603 --> 00:03:37.288
It is believed that the dutch
are actually the ones who

00:03:37.288 --> 00:03:39.528
brought the donut to America.

00:03:39.528 --> 00:03:40.566
During that time actually,

00:03:40.566 --> 00:03:42.090
donuts were not called donuts,

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.061
they were called,

00:03:43.061 --> 00:03:44.455
the translation is, "Oily cakes."

00:03:44.455 --> 00:03:45.372
- Say the word though.

00:03:45.372 --> 00:03:47.012
- I think it's olykoeks.

00:03:47.012 --> 00:03:48.662
Olykoeks.

00:03:48.662 --> 00:03:50.254
Olykecks.

00:03:50.254 --> 00:03:51.981
- I like when a name for something

00:03:51.981 --> 00:03:53.809
is just literally what it is.

00:03:53.809 --> 00:03:55.892
- It's like manslaughter.

00:03:58.795 --> 00:04:02.070
- We're going now to a very
different donut experience.

00:04:02.070 --> 00:04:04.026
And this time it's a Brioche doughnut.

00:04:04.026 --> 00:04:05.379
- Does fancier mean better?

00:04:05.379 --> 00:04:06.374
This is what we do.

00:04:06.374 --> 00:04:07.207
We find out.

00:04:07.207 --> 00:04:08.957
We're the Fancy Boys.

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.494
- Welcome to The Church Key,

00:04:16.494 --> 00:04:18.048
I'm the executive chef, Ryan Ososky.

00:04:18.048 --> 00:04:20.646
We're going to be making
our brown butter glazed

00:04:20.646 --> 00:04:22.197
Brioche doughnuts today.

00:04:22.197 --> 00:04:23.874
- And how did you come up with the idea

00:04:23.874 --> 00:04:25.478
to have donut on the menu?

00:04:25.478 --> 00:04:27.144
- [Ryan] I knew I wanted
a brown butter glaze

00:04:27.144 --> 00:04:28.840
something on the menu.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.859
Our pastry chef kind of just said,

00:04:30.859 --> 00:04:32.111
"I'm going to take what chef wants,

00:04:32.111 --> 00:04:33.665
"this brown butter glaze,

00:04:33.665 --> 00:04:34.960
"and I'm going to put it on a donut."

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:36.023
And we never looked back.

00:04:36.023 --> 00:04:37.859
We have the dough that's been proofed,

00:04:37.859 --> 00:04:39.141
doubled in size.

00:04:39.141 --> 00:04:40.464
We roll it out here.

00:04:40.464 --> 00:04:41.815
We cut our donuts out.

00:04:41.815 --> 00:04:44.528
Do the second proof of the donuts,

00:04:44.528 --> 00:04:46.402
before they go in the fryer.

00:04:46.402 --> 00:04:47.913
Then we take our portion donuts,

00:04:47.913 --> 00:04:49.533
we serve three donuts.

00:04:49.533 --> 00:04:51.735
We fry them at 325 degrees,

00:04:51.735 --> 00:04:53.773
for about five minutes.

00:04:53.773 --> 00:04:55.743
We make a brown butter glaze,

00:04:55.743 --> 00:04:59.198
which is brown butter,
powdered sugar, salt, vanilla.

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:01.222
So it's going to get salty, sweet,

00:05:01.222 --> 00:05:02.639
kind of a nutty flavor,

00:05:02.639 --> 00:05:04.235
from browning the butter.

00:05:04.235 --> 00:05:07.204
I think what stands out
donuts out is the glaze,

00:05:07.204 --> 00:05:08.333
and serving them warm,

00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:10.862
I think is truthfully the deciding factor,

00:05:10.862 --> 00:05:12.704
on what makes our donuts great.

00:05:12.704 --> 00:05:16.094
- About to consume three
delicious donuts with a milk shake

00:05:16.094 --> 00:05:17.375
on the side.

00:05:17.375 --> 00:05:18.710
We're not sipping at the same time.

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:21.276
You can start, I'll go next.

00:05:21.276 --> 00:05:23.120
- I'm waiting.

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:24.647
All right, here we go.

00:05:24.647 --> 00:05:26.079
Mm, it's mostly the PB,

00:05:26.079 --> 00:05:28.444
the J is a little more hidden.

00:05:28.444 --> 00:05:30.628
But I like that it streaks
around the outside.

00:05:30.628 --> 00:05:32.125
It's a very pretty milkshake.

00:05:32.125 --> 00:05:33.516
Nice, right?

00:05:33.516 --> 00:05:35.241
- It really is like a,

00:05:35.241 --> 00:05:37.729
can you get out of my milkshake?

00:05:37.729 --> 00:05:39.076
It's nice and thick,

00:05:39.076 --> 00:05:40.911
which is what I like about it.

00:05:40.911 --> 00:05:42.518
- Let's move on.

00:05:42.518 --> 00:05:43.710
- This one is weighty.

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:45.382
Last one was fluffy.

00:05:45.382 --> 00:05:46.491
This could be a weapon.

00:05:46.491 --> 00:05:47.554
- It is very cute though.

00:05:47.554 --> 00:05:49.458
- It's such a perfect glaze.

00:05:49.458 --> 00:05:50.375
Donut bump.

00:05:52.533 --> 00:05:55.097
- Did not expect that salt hit.

00:05:55.097 --> 00:05:56.567
- I feel guilty eating this.

00:05:56.567 --> 00:05:59.754
It's like taking a bite of
a delicious stick of butter,

00:05:59.754 --> 00:06:02.424
that's coated in all of
these amazing flavors.

00:06:02.424 --> 00:06:03.735
That's how melty it is.

00:06:03.735 --> 00:06:06.070
- The icing is a little bit
bitter from the brown butter,

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:08.311
and it really makes this
a very satisfying bite.

00:06:08.311 --> 00:06:12.435
It's like an evolving
flavor story in your mouth.

00:06:12.435 --> 00:06:13.709
- It is.

00:06:13.709 --> 00:06:15.329
- Why did you--

00:06:15.329 --> 00:06:16.570
- I agreed with you.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:18.242
- Why did you moan when I said that?

00:06:18.242 --> 00:06:19.903
- I agreed with you,

00:06:19.903 --> 00:06:23.198
and it just came out that way.

00:06:23.198 --> 00:06:25.027
What'd you think?

00:06:25.027 --> 00:06:27.064
I thought after place number one,

00:06:27.064 --> 00:06:28.517
that Blinkie's would win.

00:06:28.517 --> 00:06:31.791
But now I'm like, "Okay,
got some competition."

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:35.536
- That Church Key donut opened up my mouth

00:06:35.536 --> 00:06:39.704
to a whole other avenue of
flavor called saltiness.

00:06:39.704 --> 00:06:42.181
Whatever you're eating just gets,

00:06:42.181 --> 00:06:43.654
just explodes in your mouth,

00:06:43.654 --> 00:06:46.791
bases your tongue in its flavor goo.

00:06:46.791 --> 00:06:47.790
- Ew.

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:48.623
Moving on.

00:06:48.623 --> 00:06:50.988
- Here's a fact you donut want to miss.

00:06:50.988 --> 00:06:52.368
Donut Fact.

00:06:52.368 --> 00:06:55.662
The world record for the most jam donuts

00:06:55.662 --> 00:06:57.432
consumed in one minute

00:06:57.432 --> 00:06:58.265
is three.

00:06:58.265 --> 00:06:59.237
- That's it?

00:06:59.237 --> 00:07:01.336
- Yeah, I feel like I
could beat that, easily.

00:07:01.336 --> 00:07:04.419
- We're on our way to the final spot.

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:07.710
The golden donut.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.352
I've never eaten an item
of food covered in gold.

00:07:10.352 --> 00:07:11.675
Why do I want to eat gold?

00:07:11.675 --> 00:07:12.795
It's gold.

00:07:12.795 --> 00:07:13.864
- Yeah, it's gold.

00:07:13.864 --> 00:07:14.697
- You don't eat gold.
- That's why you want

00:07:14.697 --> 00:07:15.585
to eat gold.

00:07:15.585 --> 00:07:16.418
It's gold.

00:07:24.602 --> 00:07:25.654
- Hi, I'm Joanna.

00:07:25.654 --> 00:07:27.126
I'm the assistant general manager,

00:07:27.126 --> 00:07:28.410
here at Birdies.

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:29.577
And this is Katie.

00:07:29.577 --> 00:07:30.687
- I'm the manager and sous chef,

00:07:30.687 --> 00:07:31.862
here at Birdies.

00:07:31.862 --> 00:07:33.300
- [Steven] What is this magical
place we're in right now?

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.791
- [Joanna] Basically,
everyone loves fried chicken

00:07:34.791 --> 00:07:35.688
and donuts.

00:07:35.688 --> 00:07:38.221
Our co-founder's restaurant
toward Keith Bae,

00:07:38.221 --> 00:07:39.719
and celebrity chef Jay,

00:07:39.719 --> 00:07:41.638
decided to combine those two things,

00:07:41.638 --> 00:07:43.283
and this is how they came up with it.

00:07:43.283 --> 00:07:44.959
- [Steven] You just make
fried chicken and donuts?

00:07:44.959 --> 00:07:45.889
- [Katie] Yes.

00:07:45.889 --> 00:07:47.256
- [Steven] How is that life?

00:07:47.256 --> 00:07:48.343
- It's messy.

00:07:48.343 --> 00:07:50.451
It's messy, but fun.

00:07:50.451 --> 00:07:51.783
The donut you guys will be having today

00:07:51.783 --> 00:07:53.539
is going to be a chocolate cake donut.

00:07:53.539 --> 00:07:55.727
We start off with dark chocolate dough,

00:07:55.727 --> 00:07:57.517
which we roll out, we fry off.

00:07:57.517 --> 00:07:59.389
Once it's cooled down, we cut it in half,

00:07:59.389 --> 00:08:00.884
we fill it with strawberry jam,

00:08:00.884 --> 00:08:02.022
that we make in-house.

00:08:02.022 --> 00:08:03.456
Fill the ring with Nutella.

00:08:03.456 --> 00:08:05.380
Then we spoon our champagne glaze over it,

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:07.080
and cover it with gold leaf.

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:10.291
The champagne glaze will get
absorbed into the actual dough.

00:08:10.291 --> 00:08:11.684
So you'll get a little bit of

00:08:11.684 --> 00:08:13.478
that champagne seeping into the dough.

00:08:13.478 --> 00:08:15.544
It's not just going to
be covered in the glaze.

00:08:15.544 --> 00:08:17.906
- [Steven] How does it
feel for you as a chef,

00:08:17.906 --> 00:08:19.781
laying gold on a donut.

00:08:19.781 --> 00:08:21.239
- [Katie] I think the first time I saw it,

00:08:21.239 --> 00:08:22.374
I was like, "Really?

00:08:22.374 --> 00:08:23.794
"Like we're going to do this, really?"

00:08:23.794 --> 00:08:25.986
But I guess, now that I do
it so often, it's normal.

00:08:25.986 --> 00:08:28.097
- [Steven] Steven gold
donut is not normal.

00:08:28.097 --> 00:08:29.040
I'm excited.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:30.740
But feel kind of weird.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.289
- [Andrew] Chocolate, Nutella, strawberry,

00:08:33.289 --> 00:08:35.099
champagne, gold donut.

00:08:35.099 --> 00:08:37.381
- I don't feel like anything
in my life has prepared me

00:08:37.381 --> 00:08:38.638
for this moment.

00:08:38.638 --> 00:08:40.122
- [Andrew] I'm really excited.

00:08:40.122 --> 00:08:41.689
Not specifically because it's gold,

00:08:41.689 --> 00:08:43.657
but it looks like something
that you shouldn't eat.

00:08:43.657 --> 00:08:44.816
- [Steven] Lady and the Tramp.

00:08:44.816 --> 00:08:46.060
- Absolutely not.

00:08:46.060 --> 00:08:48.873
There's no way that
your mouth and my mouth

00:08:48.873 --> 00:08:50.925
are going to exist on the same plane

00:08:50.925 --> 00:08:52.053
in time and space.

00:08:52.053 --> 00:08:54.091
- This is dense.

00:08:54.091 --> 00:08:54.924
Powerful.

00:08:54.924 --> 00:08:56.757
All right, here we go.

00:09:02.266 --> 00:09:03.199
It's like I kissed--

00:09:03.199 --> 00:09:04.449
- A leprechaun.

00:09:05.776 --> 00:09:09.276
- [Steven] It is a really moist donut too.

00:09:18.494 --> 00:09:20.205
- [Andrew] What do I do
with the gold on my fingers?

00:09:20.205 --> 00:09:21.732
- You lick it.
It feels like a waste

00:09:21.732 --> 00:09:23.329
to wipe it off.
- Don't, eat it.

00:09:23.329 --> 00:09:24.604
- [Andrew] I gotta take another bite.

00:09:24.604 --> 00:09:25.637
- [Steven] Yeah, I do too.

00:09:25.637 --> 00:09:27.355
- [Andrew] There is this
kind of alcoholic back taste,

00:09:27.355 --> 00:09:29.193
a little bit with the icing,

00:09:29.193 --> 00:09:30.435
which is really nice.

00:09:30.435 --> 00:09:31.618
- [Steven] It's a very magical experience.

00:09:31.618 --> 00:09:32.676
You're eating gold,

00:09:32.676 --> 00:09:35.525
but you're also drinking a
glass of champagne as well.

00:09:35.525 --> 00:09:37.483
- Here I have this solid gold nugget.

00:09:37.483 --> 00:09:40.267
It seems like I just
broke it off a chandelier,

00:09:40.267 --> 00:09:41.167
ate into it,

00:09:41.167 --> 00:09:43.106
turns out it's filled with jelly.

00:09:43.106 --> 00:09:47.106
That's a magic that I think
is worth experiencing.

00:09:47.106 --> 00:09:48.186
A colleague of mine,

00:09:48.186 --> 00:09:50.116
she claimed that she pooped gold.

00:09:50.116 --> 00:09:51.983
That's going to happen?

00:09:51.983 --> 00:09:53.900
- I'm really into that.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:55.913
- Great.

00:09:55.913 --> 00:09:58.913
Okay, Adam, you're getting in there.

00:10:05.655 --> 00:10:09.825
I kind of feel like my
throat is coated in the gold.

00:10:09.825 --> 00:10:14.363
Like I have kind of an itch
at the back of my throat.

00:10:14.363 --> 00:10:15.346
- I feel great.

00:10:15.346 --> 00:10:18.655
Which donut was the most worth
it at its given price point?

00:10:18.655 --> 00:10:22.265
- The Church Key was really
a special tasting donut.

00:10:22.265 --> 00:10:24.309
The salty, caramel whole.

00:10:24.309 --> 00:10:27.381
Blinkie's is probably
the most worth it for me.

00:10:27.381 --> 00:10:31.548
That basic glazed donut that
they make is just so good.

00:10:33.981 --> 00:10:35.672
Adding anything to it,

00:10:35.672 --> 00:10:37.465
it's just downhill from there.

00:10:37.465 --> 00:10:39.543
- The gold donut, one
of a kind, literally.

00:10:39.543 --> 00:10:42.649
It was legitimately a very good donut.

00:10:42.649 --> 00:10:44.159
But I gotta say,

00:10:44.159 --> 00:10:46.665
Blinkie's is also my Worth It winner.

00:10:46.665 --> 00:10:48.582
After, what, 50 years of being open?

00:10:48.582 --> 00:10:52.170
They've just completely
perfected the donut craft.

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:54.504
- Adam, who's your Worth It winner?

00:10:54.504 --> 00:10:56.527
Did we just three-way on a donut?

00:10:56.527 --> 00:10:58.297
- I think that's called a Worth It Trio.

00:10:58.297 --> 00:11:01.380
- I think it's called a Worthagatois.

00:11:02.215 --> 00:11:03.048
- No.

00:11:14.097 --> 00:11:15.347
- [Man] Oh yes.

